IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il40-nouns`
IMPORT `il40-s4-saving`

-- TESTS for section 4.  Every expected value was worked by hand from the text of s 4 and of Interpretation Law ss 3 and 21 before the module was run.
-- Hand rules: Hebrew is "the language of the State" (s 4(a)); Arabic has "a special status" (s 4(b)); the text is silent on any other language: NOTHING.
-- "In law" (s 4(b)) is the Interpretation Law's "חוק": a law of the Knesset or an Ordinance (s 3); a regulation, an Order in Council, a Government decision
-- and an administrative direction are not.  s 4(c) leaves unharmed what it reaches (a status given in practice before the commencement day) and says nothing of the rest.

§ `Tests: section 4`

§§ `s 4(a) and (b): the status`

#ASSERT `the status the Basic Law gives to` Hebrew EQUALS JUST `the language of the State`
#ASSERT `the status the Basic Law gives to` Arabic EQUALS JUST `a special status in the State`
#ASSERT `the status the Basic Law gives to` English EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the status the Basic Law gives to` `Another language` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4(b): "in law"`

#ASSERT `s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `a law of the Knesset`
#ASSERT `s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `a Basic Law`
#ASSERT `s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `an Ordinance given before the State was established or by the Provisional Council of State`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `an Order in Council of the Mandate`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `a regulation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `a decision of the Government`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(b) counts as law an instrument of the kind` `an administrative direction`)

§§ `s 4(c): the provisions the bundle shows, and whether the Basic Law names them`

#ASSERT NOT (`art 82 of the Palestine Order in Council 1922`'s `the Basic Law names it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 15(b) of the Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948`'s `the Basic Law names it`)
#ASSERT `art 82 of the Palestine Order in Council 1922`'s `its kind` EQUALS `an Order in Council of the Mandate`
#ASSERT `s 15(b) of the Law and Administration Ordinance 5708-1948`'s `its kind` EQUALS `an Ordinance given before the State was established or by the Provisional Council of State`

§§ `s 4(c): the commencement day, by reading`

#ASSERT `the day the Basic Law commenced, reading it as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS JUST (Date 19 7 2018)
#ASSERT `the day the Basic Law commenced, reading it as` `the day it was published` EQUALS JUST (Date 26 7 2018)
#ASSERT `the day the Basic Law commenced, reading it as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 18 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 19 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 20 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 20 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 26 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 27 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 18 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 20 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a status held on` (Date 27 7 2018) `was held before the Basic Law commenced, reading the commencement day as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 4(c): the saving, by the three readings of what it saves and the three of the commencement day`

`a status given in practice in 2000` MEANS `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` WITH `it was given in practice` IS TRUE, `an enactment gave it` IS FALSE, `the day it was held` IS (Date 1 1 2000)
`a status an enactment gave in 2000, not given in practice` MEANS `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` WITH `it was given in practice` IS FALSE, `an enactment gave it` IS TRUE, `the day it was held` IS (Date 1 1 2000)
`a status given neither in practice nor by an enactment in 2000` MEANS `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` WITH `it was given in practice` IS FALSE, `an enactment gave it` IS FALSE, `the day it was held` IS (Date 1 1 2000)
`a status given in practice in 2019` MEANS `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` WITH `it was given in practice` IS TRUE, `an enactment gave it` IS FALSE, `the day it was held` IS (Date 1 1 2019)
`a status given in practice on 20 July 2018` MEANS `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` WITH `it was given in practice` IS TRUE, `an enactment gave it` IS FALSE, `the day it was held` IS (Date 20 7 2018)

#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice in 2000` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice in 2000` `, reading what it saves as` `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice in 2000` `, reading what it saves as` `what s 4(c) saves is declined` `and the commencement day as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status an enactment gave in 2000, not given in practice` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status an enactment gave in 2000, not given in practice` `, reading what it saves as` `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status an enactment gave in 2000, not given in practice` `, reading what it saves as` `what s 4(c) saves is declined` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given neither in practice nor by an enactment in 2000` `, reading what it saves as` `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice in 2019` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice on 20 July 2018` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was passed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice on 20 July 2018` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the day it was published` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(c) leaves unharmed the status` `a status given in practice on 20 July 2018` `, reading what it saves as` `only a status given in practice` `and the commencement day as` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS NOTHING
